<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Mughith Umar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1263</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Mughith Umar was the last Ayyubid ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-karak">Kerak</a>, in Transjordan, from 1250 to 1263. A grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-kamil">al-Kamil</a>, he made the fortress a refuge for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> dissidents and twice tried to invade <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> against the new Mamluk regime. In 1263 Sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> lured him out of Kerak, arrested him and had him put to death, and the castle passed to the Mamluks.</p></div>
